Krita Nova 19 - faster Transform tool

The Transform tool's in-stack preview ("Accurate" / "Accurate with Instant
Preview", the default) re-transforms the whole layer on every update (at
most every 30 ms), with the chosen filter, on a single thread. On a big
canvas that makes dragging the handles lag.

1. KisTransformWorker::transformPass() (the two resampling passes of every
   scale/rotate/shear): lines (columns in the vertical pass) are independent
   and only write to themselves, so passes of 128+ lines are split into
   chunks processed on up to 8 threads (QThread::idealThreadCount()). Tile
   access is thread-safe (filters process one device from many threads);
   the weights buffer and the applicator are only read. Same result, faster
   on multi-core CPUs (tablets have 8 cores). This also speeds up Scale
   Image/Layer, Rotate, Shear and transform masks, which use the same worker.
2. InplaceTransformStrokeStrategy::reapplyTransform(): the low-resolution
   (level of detail) preview uses the bilinear filter instead of e.g. the
   default bicubic or Lanczos3. That preview is thrown away: when the
   transform is applied it is redone at full resolution with the chosen
   filter, so the result does not change.

